HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ccoollrrmm utility first appeared in 1BSD.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     Jeff Schriebman wrote the original version of ccoollrrmm in November 1974.

BBUUGGSS
     If two characters of different widths are followed by two backspace char‐
     acters in a row, the column count is decremented twice by the width of
     the second character rather than by the sum of both widths.  This is
     hardly a practical problem because not even backspace encoding in roff(7)
     style uses such double-backspace sequences.

